<section class="cs__sec" aria-labelledby="s1">
  <p class="st-k rv">01 · Challenge</p>
  <h2 class="cs__h rv" id="s1">Many questions, scattered answers</h2>
  <p class="cs__p rv">
    Choosing a healthcare provider starts with practical questions. When the answers are hard to
    find, visitors work harder to understand the center and decide what to do next.
  </p>
  <div class="st-grid st-g4 st-wide">
    <div class="pcard rv">
      <p class="pcard__word">Question 01</p>
      <h3 class="pcard__title">Services</h3>
      <p class="pcard__text">What services and diagnostic tests are available?</p>
    </div>
    <div class="pcard rv">
      <p class="pcard__word">Question 02</p>
      <h3 class="pcard__title">Doctors</h3>
      <p class="pcard__text">Which doctors are associated with the center?</p>
    </div>
    <div class="pcard rv">
      <p class="pcard__word">Question 03</p>
      <h3 class="pcard__title">Departments</h3>
      <p class="pcard__text">Which department can address a particular need?</p>
    </div>
    <div class="pcard rv">
      <p class="pcard__word">Question 04</p>
      <h3 class="pcard__title">Contact</h3>
      <p class="pcard__text">Where can visitors find contact and appointment information?</p>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="st-callout rv">
    <p class="st-bh">
      How might we make healthcare information easier to discover, and help visitors move from
      browsing to taking action?
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="cs__sec" aria-labelledby="s2">
  <p class="st-k rv">02 · Research and discovery</p>
  <h2 class="cs__h rv" id="s2">Learning from established healthcare sites</h2>
  <p class="cs__p rv">
    I ran a competitor and benchmark analysis of healthcare and diagnostic websites. I used them to
    spot useful patterns, not as templates to copy.
  </p>
  <h3 class="st-sub rv">Six areas I compared</h3>
  <ol class="st-list st-wide rv">
    <li>Navigation and information hierarchy</li>
    <li>Doctor and department discovery</li>
    <li>How diagnostic services are presented</li>
    <li>Appointment calls to action</li>
    <li>Contact and communication options</li>
    <li>Visual consistency and trust</li>
  </ol>
  <h3 class="st-sub rv">Three principles that came out of it</h3>
  <div class="st-grid st-g3 st-wide">
    <div class="pcard rv">
      <p class="pcard__word">Principle 01</p>
      <h3 class="pcard__title">Easy to scan</h3>
      <p class="pcard__text">Healthcare information should be quick to read and compare.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="pcard rv">
      <p class="pcard__word">Principle 02</p>
      <h3 class="pcard__title">Actions within reach</h3>
      <p class="pcard__text">Booking or calling should always be easy to find.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="pcard rv">
      <p class="pcard__word">Principle 03</p>
      <h3 class="pcard__title">Essentials first</h3>
      <p class="pcard__text">Visitors should not dig through complexity to reach what matters.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
  <p class="st-note rv">
    Research was competitor and benchmark analysis only, with no patient interviews, usability
    testing or quantitative research.
  </p>
</section>

<section class="cs__sec" aria-labelledby="s3">
  <p class="st-k rv">03 · Defining the experience</p>
  <h2 class="cs__h rv" id="s3">Six pages, one clear purpose each</h2>
  <p class="cs__p rv">
    The research and requirements led to six core pages, each with one job, sharing the same set of
    patterns across the site.
  </p>
  <div class="st-stats st-wide rv">
    <div>
      <p class="st-stat">6</p>
      <p>core pages, each with one job</p>
    </div>
    <div>
      <p class="st-stat">4</p>
      <p>key UX decisions</p>
    </div>
    <div>
      <p class="st-stat">3</p>
      <p>patterns on every page: header, page banner with breadcrumbs, closing call to action</p>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="st-grid st-g3 st-wide">
    <div class="pcard rv">
      <p class="pcard__word">Page 01</p>
      <h3 class="pcard__title">Homepage</h3>
      <p class="pcard__text">Introduce the center and guide visitors to key information and actions.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="pcard rv">
      <p class="pcard__word">Page 02</p>
      <h3 class="pcard__title">About</h3>
      <p class="pcard__text">Communicate the organization’s identity, background and parent group.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="pcard rv">
      <p class="pcard__word">Page 03</p>
      <h3 class="pcard__title">Doctors</h3>
      <p class="pcard__text">Help visitors explore doctor profiles and professional information.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="pcard rv">
      <p class="pcard__word">Page 04</p>
      <h3 class="pcard__title">Departments</h3>
      <p class="pcard__text">Show the center’s areas of service, one department at a time.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="pcard rv">
      <p class="pcard__word">Page 05</p>
      <h3 class="pcard__title">Services</h3>
      <p class="pcard__text">Present diagnostic services in a structured, discoverable way.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="pcard rv">
      <p class="pcard__word">Page 06</p>
      <h3 class="pcard__title">Contact</h3>
      <p class="pcard__text">Make it straightforward to find contact details and reach the center.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="cs__sec" aria-labelledby="s4">
  <p class="st-k rv">04 · Key UX decisions</p>
  <h2 class="cs__h rv" id="s4">Four decisions that shape the site</h2>
  <p class="cs__p rv">
    Each decision answers a question visitors arrive with. Follow a typical visit first, then see
    each decision beside the screen it shaped.
  </p>

  <h3 class="st-sub rv">Visitor journey: from first visit to getting in touch</h3>
  <div class="st-wide st-tabset--steady rv">
    <div class="st-tabs" role="tablist" aria-label="Visitor journey steps">
      <button class="st-tab" type="button" role="tab" id="t-j1" aria-controls="p-j1">1. Land on the homepage</button>
      <button class="st-tab" type="button" role="tab" id="t-j2" aria-controls="p-j2">2. Find a department</button>
      <button class="st-tab" type="button" role="tab" id="t-j3" aria-controls="p-j3">3. Choose a doctor</button>
      <button class="st-tab" type="button" role="tab" id="t-j4" aria-controls="p-j4">4. Read the profile</button>
      <button class="st-tab" type="button" role="tab" id="t-j5" aria-controls="p-j5">5. Book or call</button>
    </div>
    <div class="st-gal" role="tabpanel" id="p-j1" aria-labelledby="t-j1">
      <p class="cs__p">Quick links under the hero and a services overview point straight to each part of the site.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="st-gal" role="tabpanel" id="p-j2" aria-labelledby="t-j2">
      <p class="cs__p">Each department card has a short description and the number of specialists.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="st-gal" role="tabpanel" id="p-j3" aria-labelledby="t-j3">
      <p class="cs__p">Search by name, filter by department and designation, or browse A to Z.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="st-gal" role="tabpanel" id="p-j4" aria-labelledby="t-j4">
      <p class="cs__p">
        Present institute, education and degree come first, followed by qualifications, experience,
        training, research and publications.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="st-gal" role="tabpanel" id="p-j5" aria-labelledby="t-j5">
      <p class="cs__p">Book Appointment sits beside the 10622 hotline, so visitors choose how to get in touch.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="st-split st-wide">
    <div class="st-split__text rv">
      <div class="st-decision">
        <p class="st-k">Decision A</p>
        <h3 class="st-bh">Organize information around visitor needs</h3>
        <p class="cs__p">
          Institutional information, doctors, departments and services each get their own section.
          On the homepage, quick links under the hero and a services overview point straight to
          each one.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <figure class="cs__fig rv">
      <img
        src="{{ '/assets/images/projects/akij-insaf-home.webp' | rel }}"
        width="1400"
        height="938"
        alt="Homepage section titled Complete Care, Under One Roof, with six service cards: Emergency and Urgent Care, Diagnostic and Imaging Services, Health Checkup Packages, Specialist Consultation, Day Care and Procedures, and Preventive and Wellness Care, each with a tag and a Learn more link."
        loading="lazy"
        decoding="async"
      />
      <figcaption>Homepage services overview, one route per kind of care</figcaption>
    </figure>
  </div>

  <div class="st-split st-wide">
    <div class="st-split__text rv">
      <div class="st-decision">
        <p class="st-k">Decision B</p>
        <h3 class="st-bh">Make doctor information meaningful</h3>
        <p class="cs__p">
          A profile should offer more than a name and a photo. Each one leads with the doctor’s name
          and specialty, and a summary card shows their present institute, education and degree.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <figure class="cs__fig rv">
      <img
        src="{{ '/assets/images/projects/akij-insaf-doctor-profile.webp' | rel }}"
        width="1400"
        height="1124"
        alt="Doctor profile: a photo with Present Institute, Education and Degree beneath it, then a Book Appointment button, a Hotline: 10622 button, Share Doctors Profile and a weekly schedule. On the right, the doctor's name, specialty, educational qualifications, experiences, training, research and publications."
        loading="lazy"
        decoding="async"
      />
      <figcaption>Doctor profile, professional details first</figcaption>
    </figure>
  </div>

  <div class="st-split st-wide">
    <div class="st-split__text rv">
      <div class="st-decision">
        <p class="st-k">Decision C</p>
        <h3 class="st-bh">Offer a call-center option beside Book Appointment</h3>
        <p class="cs__p">
          Not everyone wants to book online. The 10622 hotline sits right beside
          <strong>Book Appointment</strong>, and again in the top bar and the closing call to action
          on every page.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
    {#- A close-up of the doctor profile above: the summary card and the two actions under it (.st-crop--actions in story.css) #}
    <figure class="cs__fig rv">
      <div class="st-crop st-crop--actions">
        <img
          src="{{ '/assets/images/projects/akij-insaf-doctor-profile.webp' | rel }}"
          width="1400"
          height="1124"
          alt="Close-up of a doctor profile: Present Institute, Education and Degree, then a Book Appointment button with a Hotline: 10622 button directly below it."
          loading="lazy"
          decoding="async"
        />
      </div>
      <figcaption>Book Appointment and the 10622 hotline, side by side on every doctor profile</figcaption>
    </figure>
  </div>

  <div class="st-split st-wide">
    <div class="st-split__text rv">
      <div class="st-decision">
        <p class="st-k">Decision D</p>
        <h3 class="st-bh">Establish the organization’s identity</h3>
        <p class="cs__p">
          The About page explains the parent organization in one line, “A sister concern of Akij
          Insaf Group”, which links to the group’s official website.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <figure class="cs__fig rv">
      <img
        src="{{ '/assets/images/projects/akij-insaf-about.webp' | rel }}"
        width="1400"
        height="998"
        alt="About page with an About AKIJ INSAF banner, then a Who We Are section titled Our Legacy Of Trust and Compassion, two paragraphs about the center, and a link reading A sister concern of Akij Insaf Group, beside a photo of a laboratory."
        loading="lazy"
        decoding="async"
      />
      <figcaption>About page, linking to the parent group</figcaption>
    </figure>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="cs__sec" aria-labelledby="s5">
  <p class="st-k rv">05 · Visual design direction</p>
  <h2 class="cs__h rv" id="s5">Calm, clear and trustworthy</h2>
  <p class="cs__p rv">
    The goal was not visual complexity. The design supports the content and shows visitors where to
    go next: brand navy carries the header and primary actions, and red is kept for emergency and
    hotline cues.
  </p>
  {#- Palette tiles: the brand colour large, the others beside it. --sw is the tile colour;
      st-sw--dark gives light text on a dark tile. #}
  <div class="st-pal st-wide rv">
    <div class="st-sw st-sw--main st-sw--dark" style="--sw: #1b2b6d">
      <b>Brand navy</b>
      <span>HEX #1B2B6D<br />R:27 G:43 B:109</span>
    </div>
    <div class="st-sw st-sw--dark" style="--sw: #bb0000">
      <b>Heroic red</b>
      <span>HEX #BB0000<br />R:187 G:0 B:0</span>
    </div>
    <div class="st-sw" style="--sw: #f1f1fb">
      <b>Soft tint</b>
      <span>HEX #F1F1FB<br />R:241 G:241 B:251</span>
    </div>
    <div class="st-sw st-sw--wide" style="--sw: #ffffff">
      <b>White</b>
      <span>HEX #FFFFFF<br />R:255 G:255 B:255</span>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="st-grid st-g3 st-wide">
    <div class="pcard rv">
      <p class="pcard__word">Hierarchy</p>
      <h3 class="pcard__title">Clear levels</h3>
      <p class="pcard__text">Page titles, sections and supporting information each read at a distinct level.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="pcard rv">
      <p class="pcard__word">Consistency</p>
      <h3 class="pcard__title">Same patterns on six pages</h3>
      <p class="pcard__text">Typography, spacing and structured content repeat across the whole site.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="pcard rv">
      <p class="pcard__word">Actions</p>
      <h3 class="pcard__title">Important actions stand out</h3>
      <p class="pcard__text">Booking and calling are placed prominently wherever visitors need them.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

